0..70 Comment "// One ascription path for a module and a theory (#746): a module is a"
71..144 Comment "// model of a theory, `module M : Model(T)` ascribes it transparently and"
145..219 Comment "// `module M :> Model(T)` seals it, the theory\'s sorts abstract outside. A"
220..291 Comment "// theory with no laws is an ML signature; the same ascription checks a"
292..368 Comment "// theory with laws, whose members are the module\'s proofs. After Kaposi and"
369..434 Comment "// Xie (_Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories_, FSCD 2024,"
435..502 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10), whose first-order models are a"
503..573 Comment "// theory\'s algebras, and Rossberg, Russo and Dreyer (_F-ing Modules_,"
574..641 Comment "// doi:10.1017/S0956796814000264) for sealing as opaque ascription."
643..714 Comment "/// A counter: a carrier, a start and a step. No laws: an ML signature."
